{{Quote|A tough melee fighter. The Barbarian's handsome, cultured cousin. Rumor has it that he was knighted based on the sheer awesomeness of his mustache alone.}}

The Super Knight was a temporary {{Rarity|Legendary}} [[Cards|card]], only available in certain Events. It spawned a single-target, ground-targeting, melee, ground troop with high hitpoints and moderate damage. When he moves forward and doesn't attack, he and any allies within an 8 tiles radius around himself receive 1 damage from all sources. A Super Knight card cost 4 [[Elixir]] to deploy.

== Strategy ==

* Unlike the [[Knight/Evolution|Evolved Knight]], which reduces damage done to himself from all sources by 60%, all forms of damage done to the Super Knight and all nearby friendly troops, including towers, will be reduced to 1, making the card and whatever surrounds him within a 6 tile radius essentially unkillable when moving.
** Units with a very high attack speed like [[Mighty Miner]], [[Little Prince]], [[Inferno Dragon]], [[Dart Goblin]], [[Lumberjack]], [[Three Musketeers]], [[Barbarians/Evolution|Evolved Barbarians]], [[Golden Knight]], [[Monk]], and [[Berserker]] are slightly more effective at dealing damage to troops protected by the Super Knight, but unless they're at critical health, it's still very ineffective. Even a [[Skeletons|Skeleton]] will still take multiple minutes to destroy.
** [[Clone|Cloned]] troops and the [[Skeleton King]]'s Skeletons will always have 1 HP. From this, the Super Knight’s damage reduction will not change any interactions, allowing these troops to still die in one hit from anything.
* The Super Knight's damage reduction will deactivate once he starts attacking and reactivates once there aren't any enemies in range and he starts moving again. Because of this, it's better to play the Super Knight at the back of a push. Thus, it will take longer for the Knight to reach the enemies and ensure his protection lasts longer.
* Light ground swarms, like [[Guards]], [[Skeletons/Evolution|Evolved Skeletons]], [[Goblin Gang]], and [[Skeleton Army]] synergize very effectively with the Super Knight. Due to the Super Knight's protection making it impossible to eliminate them in one hit, these swarms can more easily take advantage of their high DPS. This damage reduction can significantly assist them in taking out unprotected enemy troops, preventing the Super Knight from attacking anything.
* To counter the Super Knight, it’s essential to deploy a ground card with high DPS directly on top of him to deactivate his damage reduction as soon as possible.
** The [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.|Mini P.E.K.K.A]] and [[Super Mini P.E.K.K.A.|Super Mini P.E.K.K.A]] are perfect examples of reliable counters to the Super Knight. Not only will they deactivate his damage reduction, but will also destroy him and counterattack with nearly full hitpoints leftover for a respectable cost.
** Light ground swarms like [[Skeleton Army]] are unreliable, but effective counters to him. Their low hitpoints makes them extremely susceptible to [[Rage]], a common synergy with the Super Knight, that will instantly destroy the swarm and keep the Super Knight alive. However, if a small spell isn’t used, they can take him out for a positive Elixir trade.
** Air cards, even [[Inferno Dragon]], are completely incapable of dealing with the Super Knight in any way while he’s moving. Their flying status keeps them from distracting the Super Knight, which in turn keeps his damage reduction from deactivating.
*In the scenario that the player has cycled back to a Super Knight, it’s highly recommended to deploy the two Super Knights within range of each other's damage reduction. Once one Super Knight starts attacking, the other Super Knight will continue to protect him as long as he stays moving, buying the other Super Knight more time to reactivate his damage reduction.
*If a Super Mini P.E.K.K.A. reaches a [[:Category:Crown Towers|Crown Tower]], the Super Knight could be played as a last ditch effort to protect the Crown Tower from being instantly destroyed. Even then, his chance of survival is still low as the Knight's damage reduction will soon be lifted from the Crown Tower if he moves out of range or starts attacking an enemy unit.
*The [[Goblin Curse]] is the only card capable of mitigating the Super Knight's damage reduction, allowing you to deal 20% damage to them. High DPS troops should be used to take advantage of the Goblin Curse because of this. For example, If the attacking Super Knight is surrounded by a Skeleton Army, you can counter it by playing your own Super Knight and Skeleton Army in addition to deploying the Goblin Curse on the enemy's Skeletons. This allows your own Skeletons to take out the enemy Skeletons without taking as much damage, which in turn transform into your own Goblins. These Goblins then will help intensify your counterattack.
** Due to the Goblin Curse transforming opposing troops into Goblins, there’s a good chance that the enemy Super Knight will start attacking the spawned Goblins. This will deactivate his damage reduction and allow for him to be quickly defeated.

